To properly incorporate the `CWD` (Change Working Directory) and `MLSD` (Machine Listing Directory) commands into the sequence of client requests, we need to consider where these commands logically fit in the workflow. Typically, you would change to the desired directory after listing the contents or before creating a new directory.

Here is a modified version of your sequence, including `CWD` and `MLSD`:

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,132,209
LIST
CWD test         # Change to the newly created directory "test"
MLSD              # List the contents of the "test" directory
MKD test         # Create a new directory named "test"
QUIT
```

This sequence assumes that you want to change to the "test" directory after listing the contents of the current directory and before creating a new directory. If you meant to create the directory first and then list it, you would adjust the order accordingly. Here's an alternative version:

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,132,209
LIST
MKD test         # Create a new directory named "test"
CWD test         # Change to the newly created directory "test"
MLSD              # List the contents of the "test" directory
QUIT
```

Choose the sequence that best fits your intended workflow!

